.TH CHANGED 1 "2026-10-24" "cools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
changed \- list files modified since a date or within N days
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changed
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR] (\fB--days\fR \fIN\fR | \fB--since\fR \fIDATE\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively scan a directory and print files modified after the given cutoff.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --days N
Files modified in the last N days.
.TP
.B --since DATE
Files modified since DATE (YYYY-MM-DD[ HH:MM[:SS]]).
.SH OUTPUT
MTIME_EPOCH<TAB>PATH
.SH EXAMPLES
changed . --days 7
.SH SEE ALSO
bigfiles(1), fileinfo(1), contextpack(1)
